# ==============================================================================
# Why Exclude Each Category
# ==============================================================================

# __pycache__/ (~20-50MB):
# - Generated during runtime
# - Python bytecode files
# - Will be recreated automatically

# venv/ (~100-200MB):
# - Will be created fresh in builder stage
# - Ensures consistent dependencies
# - Reduces build context significantly

# .env* (contains secrets):
# - Never include secrets in Docker image
# - Prevents credential leakage
# - Environment-specific, not portable

# .git/ (~50-200MB):
# - Git history not needed
# - Prevents credential leakage
# - Reduces build context size

# .pytest_cache/, .coverage (~10-20MB):
# - Test artifacts not needed in production
# - Reduces image size
# - Faster builds

# dist/, build/ (~10-50MB):
# - Build artifacts from local development
# - Will be generated fresh in container
# - Not needed in production

# ==============================================================================
# Build Context Impact
# ==============================================================================

# Without .dockerignore:
# - Build context: ~200MB
# - Transfer time: 5-15 seconds
# - Includes: venv, __pycache__, .git, tests, etc.

# With .dockerignore:
# - Build context: ~5MB
# - Transfer time: <1 second
# - Includes: Only app/ source code and requirements.txt
# - Reduction: 97%

# Verify build context size:
#   docker build --progress=plain -t test:latest . 2>&1 | grep "Sending build context"

# ==============================================================================
# Negation Patterns (Advanced)
# ==============================================================================

# To exclude all .env files but include .env.example:
# .env*
# !.env.example

# To exclude all tests but include specific file:
# test_*.py
# !test_critical.py

# To exclude venv except specific package:
# venv/
# !venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/critical-package/

# ==============================================================================
# Pattern Syntax
# ==============================================================================

# *.log        - All .log files in current directory only
# **/*.log     - All .log files recursively (any depth)
# logs/        - Entire logs directory
# !important   - Include file/directory (negation)

# ==============================================================================
# Required Files for Build
# ==============================================================================

# These files MUST be present (not excluded):
# - requirements.txt (Python dependencies)
# - app/ (application source code)
# - pyproject.toml (if using Poetry - configure separately)

# Typical backend/ directory structure sent to Docker:
# backend/
# ├── requirements.txt (~1KB)
# ├── app/
# │   ├── __init__.py
# │   ├── main.py
# │   ├── database.py
# │   ├── models/
# │   ├── routers/
# │   └── utils/
# └── [.dockerignore excludes everything else]

# ==============================================================================
# Testing .dockerignore
# ==============================================================================

# Build with verbose output to see context size:
#   docker build --progress=plain -t backend:test ./backend 2>&1 | head -n 20

# Check what files are sent to Docker daemon:
#   docker build --no-cache -t backend:test ./backend 2>&1 | grep -i "sending"

# Expected output with proper .dockerignore:
#   Sending build context to Docker daemon: 5.2MB

# List files in build context (advanced):
#   tar -c . --exclude-vcs --exclude='Dockerfile*' | tar -t | wc -l
#   # Should be < 100 files for typical FastAPI project

# ==============================================================================
# Python-Specific Exclusions
# ==============================================================================

# Why exclude __pycache__:
# - Generated automatically by Python
# - Version-specific (Python 3.13 vs 3.12)
# - Will be recreated in container
# - Can cause issues if copied from different Python version

# Why exclude venv:
# - Local development environment
# - May contain platform-specific binaries
# - Different from /opt/venv created in Docker
# - Reduces context by ~100-200MB

# Why exclude .pytest_cache:
# - Test execution cache
# - Not needed for production
# - Will be regenerated if tests run in container

# ==============================================================================
# FastAPI-Specific Exclusions
# ==============================================================================

# Why exclude alembic/ migrations:
# - Database migrations run separately
# - Not needed in application container
# - Version-controlled separately
# - Run via migration jobs, not application startup

# Why exclude *.db, *.sqlite:
# - Local development databases
# - Production uses external PostgreSQL (Neon)
# - Prevents accidental data inclusion in image

# ==============================================================================
# Security Considerations
# ==============================================================================

# Never include:
# - .env files (secrets)
# - *.key, *.pem (SSL certificates)
# - credentials.json (service accounts)
# - Any file with passwords or API keys

# Best practices:
# - Use runtime environment variables
# - Use Docker secrets in production
# - Use Kubernetes secrets for orchestration
# - Rotate secrets regularly

# ==============================================================================
# Maintenance Notes
# ==============================================================================

# Review and update .dockerignore when:
# - Adding new Python packages
# - Changing project structure
# - Adding new development tools
# - Noticing slow build context transfers

# Regular audit:
#   docker build --progress=plain . 2>&1 | grep "Sending build context"
#   # Should be < 10MB for typical FastAPI project

# Compare with git-tracked files:
#   git ls-files backend/ | wc -l
#   # Build context should have similar or fewer files

# ==============================================================================
# Performance Impact
# ==============================================================================

# Excluding large directories significantly improves:
# 1. Build context transfer speed (95%+ faster)
# 2. Docker build time (no processing of excluded files)
# 3. Cache invalidation (only source code changes matter)
# 4. CI/CD pipeline speed (faster context upload)

# Benchmark:
# - Without .dockerignore: 15-30 seconds context transfer
# - With .dockerignore: <1 second context transfer
# - Time savings: 95%+ on every build
